<title>USA: Fidelity accused of SEC violations in lawsuit.</title>
<headline>Fidelity accused of SEC violations in lawsuit.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fidelity Brokerage Services Inc was named in a class action lawsuit filed Tuesday on behalf of all holders of warrants to buy common shares through Fidelity in the Schuller Corp predecessor company Manville Corp nearly one year ago.</p>
<p>A spokesman for Fidelity said the financial services firm had not seen the lawsuit, adding he had no comment.</p>
<p>An attorney representing at least one plaintiff in the suit said Fidelity's alleged failure to notify the plaintiff class it had a deadline of April 8, 1996 to convert the warrants into common stock prevented them from receiving a special dividend of $6 a share paid by Manville April 12, 1996.</p>
<p>The attorney said the lawsuit does not include Schuller.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
